{#
  ══ WITHDRAWING REFERRAL EARNINGS ═══════════════════════════════════════════════

  A partial, because it is the one part of /account that is a FORM about money and it has
  four mutually exclusive states — requested, available, blocked, and "we do not have your
  bank details yet". Inline in the page those four read as one long card with most of it
  conditionally absent, which is how the wrong one came to be shown.

  It is rendered `only`, with everything it needs passed in, so it cannot quietly start
  depending on a page variable that changes meaning.

  ── THE RULES IT ENFORCES VISUALLY ───────────────────────────────────────────────

  `payout_can` answers "can they" AND "why not" together — see `ReferralPayout::available()`
  — so this never draws a button that will refuse. An open request replaces the form
  entirely rather than sitting above it: two ways to ask for the same money is how somebody
  asks twice.

  The bank details are saved once and reused, and each payout keeps its own copy, so
  changing them never alters where an earlier transfer went. That is said out loud because
  it is the question somebody editing this form is actually asking.

  Fields are 52px with 16px text (§11, so focusing one cannot zoom the viewport on iOS) and
  carry `inputmode` and `autocomplete`. The account-number field is `inputmode="numeric"`
  and NOT `type="number"`: a leading zero is significant in a Nigerian account number and
  a number input drops it.
#}

{% if payout_open %}
  <div class="me-note me-note--ok" role="status">
    <b>₦{{ payout_open.amount_naira|number_format }} requested</b>
    {% if payout_open.requested_at %}on {{ payout_open.requested_at|slice(0,10) }}{% endif %},
    to {{ payout_open.bank_name|default('your saved account') }}{% if payout_open.account_name %} · {{ payout_open.account_name }}{% endif %}.
    We pay by bank transfer and will be in touch once it has gone.
  </div>

{% elseif payout_can %}
  <form method="post" action="/account/payout" data-ag-validate novalidate
        style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px">
    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">
    <b class="me-card__h">Withdraw ₦{{ payout_amount|number_format }} to your bank</b>
    <span class="me-sub">Paid by bank transfer, usually within a few working days. The
      account name has to match your own — a mismatch is the usual reason one is refused.</span>

    <div class="me-pay">
      <label class="sr-only" for="poBank">Bank</label>
      <input id="poBank" class="me-input" type="text" name="bank" required maxlength="120"
             autocomplete="off" placeholder="Bank (e.g. GTBank)"
             value="{{ payout_bank.bank|default('') }}">

      <label class="sr-only" for="poName">Account name</label>
      <input id="poName" class="me-input" type="text" name="account_name" required maxlength="160"
             autocomplete="name" placeholder="Account name"
             value="{{ payout_bank.account_name|default('') }}">

      <label class="sr-only" for="poNum">Account number</label>
      <input id="poNum" class="me-input" type="text" name="account_number" required
             inputmode="numeric" pattern="[0-9]*" maxlength="20" autocomplete="off"
             placeholder="Account number"
             value="{{ payout_bank.account_number|default('') }}">

      <button type="submit" class="me-btn me-btn--go" style="min-width:160px">Request payout</button>
    </div>
  </form>

{% elseif payout_why %}
  <p class="me-sub">{{ payout_why }}</p>
{% endif %}

<details class="me-card" style="padding:14px 18px"{% if not payout_bank.account_number|default('') %} open{% endif %}>
  <summary style="cursor:pointer;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;min-height:32px;display:flex;align-items:center">
    {{ payout_bank.account_number|default('') ? 'Change your bank details' : 'Save your bank details' }}
  </summary>
  <p class="me-sub" style="margin:8px 0 10px">
    Saved once and reused for every withdrawal. Each payout keeps its own copy, so changing
    these never alters where an earlier transfer went. We pay by ordinary bank transfer —
    nothing is set up on your behalf with the payment provider.
  </p>
  <form method="post" action="/account/bank" data-ag-validate novalidate>
    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">
    <div class="me-pay">
      <label class="sr-only" for="bkBank">Bank</label>
      <input id="bkBank" class="me-input" type="text" name="bank" required maxlength="120"
             autocomplete="off" placeholder="Bank (e.g. GTBank)"
             value="{{ payout_bank.bank|default('') }}">
      <label class="sr-only" for="bkName">Account name</label>
      <input id="bkName" class="me-input" type="text" name="account_name" required maxlength="160"
             autocomplete="name" placeholder="Account name — must be yours"
             value="{{ payout_bank.account_name|default('') }}">
      <label class="sr-only" for="bkNum">Account number</label>
      <input id="bkNum" class="me-input" type="text" name="account_number" required
             inputmode="numeric" pattern="[0-9]*" maxlength="20" autocomplete="off"
             placeholder="Account number"
             value="{{ payout_bank.account_number|default('') }}">
      <button type="submit" class="me-btn">Save details</button>
    </div>
  </form>
</details>

{% if payout_history|default([])|length %}
<section class="me-grp">
  <h2>Withdrawals</h2>
  <div class="me-rows">
    {% for h in payout_history %}
    <span class="me-r" data-find="payout withdrawal {{ h.status }}">
      <span class="me-r__b">
        <span class="me-r__n">₦{{ h.amount_naira|number_format }}</span>
        <span class="me-r__s">{% if h.requested_at %}{{ h.requested_at|slice(0,10) }}{% endif %}{% if h.payment_ref %} · {{ h.payment_ref }}{% endif %}{% if h.note %} · {{ h.note }}{% endif %}</span>
      </span>
      <span class="me-pill me-pill--{{ h.status == 'paid' ? 'ok' : (h.status == 'rejected' ? 'bad' : 'wait') }}">{{ h.status|capitalize }}</span>
    </span>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}
